# Migrating from 0.20 to 1.0

Treat 1.0 as a migration, not a mechanical import rename. Upwell `0.20.0` already uses the `upwell` crate and `upwell::...` module paths, but its host declaration is the pre-1.0 builder form.

## Start with the application boundary

Replace the 0.20 builder-form host declaration with the 1.0 named application declaration, then follow the current [application model](/docs/1.0.0/framework/application-model) and [`app!` guide](/docs/1.0.0/framework/app-macro) for the complete 1.0 model.

<Example title="Move the app declaration">

```rust plain
// Upwell 0.20
app! {
    App::builder("catalog")
        .with_component(Catalog)
}
```

```rust plain
// Upwell 1.0
app! {
    pub app CatalogApplication {
        name: "catalog",
    }
}
```

</Example>

The 1.0 host has a different declaration shape and can introduce protocol-specific configuration. Revisit registrations, generated process behavior, and startup commands as part of that move rather than assuming the builder chain maps option-for-option.

## Migrate by feature area

- Rebuild components and dependency injection from the [1.0 components guide](/docs/1.0.0/di/components).
- Rework HTTP code using the [1.0 HTTP controllers guide](/docs/1.0.0/axum/http).
- Rework daemon RPC code using the [1.0 RPC services guide](/docs/1.0.0/rpc/services).

Historical features can differ in their generated integration, scopes, and accepted macro forms. This guide records the 0.20 forms shown here, but does not claim compatibility for forms not documented for that release.

## Reference availability

The preserved 0.20 artifact has its own legacy symbol identity, so this site does not publish cross-version symbol-reference pages for it. Use these authored 0.20 guides for the historical package and macro forms; use the [current 1.0 reference](/docs/1.0.0/framework/application-model) only after migrating to 1.0.
